{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/tidepool","sessionId":"bf1feaa0-a7f3-49d2-bee3-93bdd89b4490","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"I keep forgetting how tide prediction works. explain harmonic constituents like I'm a programmer, short"},"uuid":"bc0e789a-f21d-4b81-89a9-459f387148de","timestamp":"2026-08-30T16:31:30.600Z"}
{"parentUuid":"bc0e789a-f21d-4b81-89a9-459f387148de","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/tidepool","sessionId":"bf1feaa0-a7f3-49d2-bee3-93bdd89b4490","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_7570c50fe0f1d2820ddcea56","message":{"id":"msg_0f4747ce85667471bfe80267","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A tide prediction is a sum of sine waves. Each constituent is one astronomical rhythm with a fixed period: M2 is the principal lunar tide (12.42 h), S2 the solar one (12.00 h), K1 and O1 are the daily lunar-solar pair. For a given station, measurements give each constituent an amplitude and a phase. Prediction is then `h(t) = mean + Σ amplitude·cos(speed·t + phase)`, a loop over about 37 terms. Spring and neap tides are just M2 and S2 drifting in and out of phase every 14.8 days."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1240,"output_tokens":83}},"uuid":"f136bfc9-ba52-4141-8b20-91e8aa905cd3","timestamp":"2026-08-30T16:32:17.380Z"}
{"parentUuid":"f136bfc9-ba52-4141-8b20-91e8aa905cd3","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/tidepool","sessionId":"bf1feaa0-a7f3-49d2-bee3-93bdd89b4490","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"so the station data is basically a list of amplitudes and phases"},"uuid":"b2a97068-3639-41b5-a917-1e1145fc8c19","timestamp":"2026-08-30T16:33:40.180Z"}
{"parentUuid":"b2a97068-3639-41b5-a917-1e1145fc8c19","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/tidepool","sessionId":"bf1feaa0-a7f3-49d2-bee3-93bdd89b4490","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_1018d9511f5571c9e87be49f","message":{"id":"msg_2616ddab62f5adf338beca7a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Exactly, plus the datum and the station's zone for display. Which is why a wrong zone gives you a perfect prediction at the wrong time: the ghost hour."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1320,"output_tokens":89}},"uuid":"2b4b9929-621b-4f3f-a563-e91d1ed332d6","timestamp":"2026-08-30T16:34:11.975Z"}
